comments.body:
@participant1 
Yes, same happens if I only set "v8_enable_sandbox = false".
This one seems to be the cause.

I'd see two ways to fix this issue:

1. This issue seems to have been introduced in v40 before it hit alpha status. So one way to find a fix would be to compile various v40 nightly builds with the gn args you used and find the commit that broke it. If it's a commit in Electron, that should make fixing it significantly easier. If it's a Chromium roll, it might not help much, unfortunately.
2. The other way would be to just jump into the Chromium/V8 code and figure out the root cause of the bug directly. Based on the stack trace from [#48699](https://github.com/electron/electron/issues/48699), [this code section](https://<redacted-host>/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:v8/include/v8-handle-base.h;l=77-80;drc=2bf85d2557208cd3f37461125f3fa5559703b721) might be a good starting point:
    ```
    // Returns the address of the actual heap object (tagged).
    // This method must be called only if the handle is not empty, otherwise it
    // will crash.
    V8_INLINE internal::Address ptr() const { return *location_; }
    ```

Quick tip: Building Electron is easier with https://github.com/electron/build-tools instead of calling `ninja` directly. (Switching requires recompiling everything though.)
